meta {
  name: Investment Holdings
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{plaidBaseUrl}}/investments/holdings/get
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "access_token": "{{plaidAccessToken}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.holdings: isDefined
  res.body.securities: isDefined
}

docs {
  The holdings and the securities they refer to. Look at each security's `ticker_symbol`:
  Plaid sends some funds with a name and **no ticker** (a target-date trust, a 529
  portfolio), and a settlement fund as a ticker-less mutual fund. The backend keeps those
  under their name behind a `#`, and reads the settlement fund as cash
  (`plaid_reader.security_symbol`, `is_cash_holding`).
}
